      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m confused about this change... or rather, I\u0027m confused about why I introduced the suffix to start with. It\u0027s there to guard against large literals without a type:\n\n```\n10 \u003c 3_000_000_000\n```\n\nfails to compile because the large value is inferred to be a `i32`. So for this case, the suffix is needed.\n\nLooking at the code again, this is not needed here since `max_value` will be inferred to the `backing_type` via the comparison. It seems to me that it should also be inferred correctly in the other places where we use it, so let me make a CL to remove the suffix completely.",
      "revId": "0788c3e455d20f7db4d3e9cdefb5227ec64fd678",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
